  "summary": "Hyostylic like the shark, but the head is flattened and the mouth is ventral, so the upper jaw is thrust down and forward rather than straight forward. Hypobranchial muscles that the shark has only as a coracomandibularis and coracohyoideus are extended into depressors that reach the jaw and the hyomandibula.",
